        <detaileddescription>
<para>Constructor</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>init</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Set to true if you need to initialize libcurl.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
Libcurl require us to call an initialization method once, before using the library. If you use libcurl exclusively from RESTinCurl, <computeroutput>init</computeroutput> needs to be <computeroutput>true</computeroutput> (default). If you use RESTinCurl in a project that already initialize libcurl, you should pass <computeroutput>false</computeroutput> to the constructor.</para>
<para>RESTinCurl will only call libcurl&apos;s initialization once, no matter how many times you call the constructor. It&apos;s therefore safe to always use the default value when you want RESTinCurl to deal with libcurl&apos;s initialization. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
