    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The high level abstraction of the Curl library.</para>
<para>An instance of a <ref refid="classrestincurl_1_1Client" kindref="compound">Client</ref> will, if asynchronous mode is enabled, create a worker-thread when the first request is made. This single worker-thread is then shared between all requests made for this client. When no requests are active, the thread will wait for a while (see RESTINCURL_IDLE_TIMEOUT_SEC), keeping libcurl&apos;s connection-cache warm, to serve new requests as efficiently as possible. When the idle time period expires, the thread will terminate and close the connection-cache associated with the client. If a new request is made later on, a new worker-thread will be created. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
